Twenty-four settings passed as arguments would be unreadable and difficult to extend without breaking existing calls, so they travel in a struct. The constructor calls
SetDefaults()
, so a host that needs to change only three settings can set those three and leave the rest at their defaults.
SetDefaults()
is declared before the constructor in the struct body, so the constructor can call it without relying on a member function being defined later in the struct. The five divergence fields pass straight through to the engine and keep the meanings the previous part documented. Symbol accepts an empty string, which resolves to the chart symbol during initialization.
The defaults are starting points, not values selected for this header. SARStep 0.02 and SARMaximum 0.20 are the usual Parabolic SAR settings and the defaults of the terminal's own Parabolic SAR indicator. MPOLength 6, MPOSmooth 7, RSIPeriod 14 and PivotLength 2 are the oscillator defaults this series has used since the MPO4 oscillator was introduced. AdaptFactor 0.3 and DivBarsLimit 200 are the shrink factor and the bar limit of the earlier parts, carried over unchanged. None of them was tuned for trailing, and they are best set for the instrument, the timeframe and how much room the stop should give.
The Four-Call Lifecycle
The whole integration contract is four methods:
