Two results sit outside this table because they are decided outside the proposal: PSAR_TRAIL_NOT_MINE, when a position's symbol or magic number does not belong to this instance, and PSAR_TRAIL_MODIFY_FAILED, when the server refuses a request that passed every check here.
The distance gate and the break-even guard both measure distance from the entry price. Neither accounts for commission, swap, or spread. Therefore, StartPoints movement does not guarantee account-level profit, and an entry-price stop is not necessarily break-even. On an instrument with a wide spread or a per-lot commission, the level that actually breaks even sits further out. The header has no field for those costs, so both remain price rules, and a stop the guard accepts at the entry price can still close the trade at a small loss once costs are counted.
Tick Alignment
A stop has to sit on the symbol's tick grid, or the broker may reject it. Rounding to the nearest tick is the obvious approach, but it is subtly wrong because it can move the level by up to half a tick toward price, which is precisely the direction that can cause the candidate to breach the stops level against which it is about to be measured.
